abstract: >-
  We construct an internal gauge–matter response system and prove a positive
  spectral gap for its generated Yang–Mills operator from minimal unbiased
  compositional change. Independent composition and square-root scaling with
  unit covariance fix a centred Gaussian law on the least-dimensional compact
  connected faithful irreducible orthogonal carrier. Its ladder operations and
  coherent comparisons generate the round SU(2) process spectrum. Complete
  centre-invariant observations give RP³. The relative-frame continuation
  together with the least-matter and elementary-connector continuations
  preserves the generated adjoint and exchange structures and the source phase
  and reversal. They determine (SU(3)× SU(2)× U(1))/ℤ₆ acting on a
  sixteen-dimensional full matter module with a fifteen-dimensional charged
  quotient. The elementary connector has one complex scalar doublet
  coordinate. The colour connection supplies the collective intensity together
  with Casimir feedback and the long-root drive. The complete spectral
  response has a unique positive equilibrium at the source-calibrated IR
  radius L_src=√(2π)>L_c=√π. Its normalized radial curvature and common-frame
  coexact response form the Yang–Mills mass operator. Its equilibrium Gaussian
  response completion has a unique vacuum and an attained positive gap. The
  original connection polynomials retain their source state and products under
  the intertwined equilibrium update. The curvature mean has a nonzero radial
  differential. The first source corner also generates a Lorentz event carrier
  and a phase clock. Osterwalder–Schrader reconstruction gives free local
  fields. Native vertices admit causal perturbative reconstruction at
  gauge-compatible finite internal resolution. Anomaly cancellation gives the
  physical BRST net at every perturbative order in the renormalizable
  gauge–matter realization. In the quadratic field realization colour
  intensity has a radial pole and explicit multiparticle continua.
